                        "sense_id": "ef1629dc-bd1c-32e0-857f-bb7cf8f681e2",
                        "entry_id": "034782fe-402d-3baf-8845-b850946a820b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who pretends to be wise; a wiseacre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "db5e1876-8838-465d-b4ad-fb209385c3ee",
                                "sense_id": "ef1629dc-bd1c-32e0-857f-bb7cf8f681e2",
                                "text": "This may well put to the blush those wiselings that show themselves fools in so speaking. ― Donne."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d7cd177e-d134-43b0-9bb4-b5c06135ed34",
                                "sense_id": "ef1629dc-bd1c-32e0-857f-bb7cf8f681e2",
                                "text": "This is the book that makes fools of little wiselings."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9787b6d0-331f-4798-b5c6-00c259d6e33d",
                                "sense_id": "ef1629dc-bd1c-32e0-857f-bb7cf8f681e2",
                                "text": "What! a score o' wiselings, and not one to hit oot the means and the way?\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "08b33071-8712-446a-84b3-0426e893831c",
                                "sense_id": "ef1629dc-bd1c-32e0-857f-bb7cf8f681e2",
                                "text": "A wiseling keeps his real sentiments on this point to himself – guards them as his own life. The best mask for moral heresy is one of pretended sanctity."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
